#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace Spanned by Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23a80ebd-83ac-57fe-8d29-cf9d378a55e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324264} {:answer/id #uuid "8e054025-c750-507e-b378-275bfa2cff6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325176} {:answer/id #uuid "c69c4434-a2aa-5d28-8313-b21b21c08cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325687} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6d1a6a-9da2-5d83-aa2c-926093703b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325754} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f6656e-2e27-5295-8486-ecf5d17ab06b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd6d1a6a-9da2-5d83-aa2c-926093703b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325754} :answer-field/id #uuid "e806f62c-89ec-51c4-a668-7516a58964fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c22b52e6-cf75-58b2-823a-b76f6234d620" :question/math-academy-id "q-40610" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 4}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}}{a}_{1}=(-\\frac{2}{3})\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3})\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{4}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x$ coincides with the projection, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is zero $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335b9523-deca-5d75-9645-1d6c085346a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348905} {:answer/id #uuid "3e46f765-0b2a-5a5b-aa2f-fe57b7223392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349016} {:answer/id #uuid "7896d87f-1a14-5e41-95b9-5be658f8e426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349560} {:answer/id #uuid "d873db20-5652-56e2-8e0e-3fce4bf0bc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350343} {:answer/id #uuid "dd092b3c-8771-57e2-8990-445d555aa3f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "335b9523-deca-5d75-9645-1d6c085346a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348905} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9fe258c-56e4-5ca0-ba85-c092749a9d1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf535ed1-7a3f-5586-9dd6-0d4749a3c85c" :question/math-academy-id "q-81591" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}v=-1\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}w=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8597217-e879-5a91-9607-1c6b8944ba4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373287} {:answer/id #uuid "efef12bf-f408-5a25-a456-76ad7d94c94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373288} {:answer/id #uuid "51f1110f-3c18-55c8-9ec1-6788d97a8d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373289} {:answer/id #uuid "45f7982a-75cc-575c-857b-dedc45e412a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373290} {:answer/id #uuid "518c875c-654e-5b51-80ed-b82ea095d7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "518c875c-654e-5b51-80ed-b82ea095d7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373291} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f3a843-28a3-51eb-bedb-cdde55c51606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4faefb01-3257-5fa8-9e41-d2b284e76cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-81594" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{15\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 6+(-3)\\cdot (-12)}{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-12)^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{15\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace Spanned by Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28faabea-dfd0-55c2-85b3-adad07d107a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348800} {:answer/id #uuid "55e962b4-4213-584d-8bfc-bfbc26a4d99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349233} {:answer/id #uuid "700d4add-8f9b-56f7-9ad3-952853092eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349476} {:answer/id #uuid "7a977362-a0b9-5918-829f-9fcce5294908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349574} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b37dbd-c83f-534f-9dde-b0d19a5de4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28faabea-dfd0-55c2-85b3-adad07d107a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348800} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbf28350-f1e7-50ad-82d9-dcc4233c0637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb8dc59e-a778-5f61-ad00-84a88b09a301" :question/math-academy-id "q-82912" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 2}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\hat{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\hat{x}) & =‖x-\\hat{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\hat{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\hat{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\hat{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\hat{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-3)^{2}+(3-3)^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133787 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace Spanned by Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "595c7e06-3764-50ba-bec9-2bb2d3ec8790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349268} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8e37ce-0b65-547d-84ec-59a0dfaca58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349307} {:answer/id #uuid "61659e8c-dc0c-5345-8f4d-2a2cf2f10dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349339} {:answer/id #uuid "da60a60e-ab26-511f-89ca-0c3669b393ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350363} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ee56a9-520e-5f79-93b1-b6aa6e6c7618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da60a60e-ab26-511f-89ca-0c3669b393ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350363} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac760160-44fe-5b46-87a9-67bd6bc761bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "938eaa8d-afe0-5769-ad70-d905f6708ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-82914" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\hat{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\hat{x}) & =‖x-\\hat{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\hat{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\hat{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\hat{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\hat{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2-\\frac{9}{4})}^{2}+{(1-(-\\frac{3}{4}))}^{2}+{(-3-(-\\frac{7}{4}))}^{2}+{(1-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{49}{16}+\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{1}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{76}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
